WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:05.870
Life at the SCP Foundation isn't exactly made
up of sunshine and rainbows.

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:09.999
It's less of a "good vibes" kind of place,
and more of a "this is the solemn work we

00:00:09.999 --> 00:00:14.840
do as we stand between humanity and the vast,
unfeeling, unknowable realm of mystery and

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:15.840
darkness."

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.790
Sure, sometimes there's a magic vending machine
or a teddy bear doctor, but most of the time

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:25.160
the Foundation's findings are a lot more bite
than they are bark.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:29.910
Thankfully, there's the "C" portion of that
infamous acronym, "Contain."

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:34.870
They keep their bizarre, astounding findings
locked up tight, where they can't catch an

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:37.760
unsuspecting innocent off guard and-

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.760
Aah!

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:39.760
Oh, hey there little buddy!

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.129
It's okay, you didn't mean to scare me.

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:47.449
Relax, everyone, it's just SCP-999, one of
the only contained curiosities allowed to

00:00:47.449 --> 00:00:50.449
roam freely around the halls of the Foundation.

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:51.530
Just look at this guy!

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:55.159
Has a sentient mass of translucent orange
slime ever been so cute?

00:00:55.159 --> 00:00:56.909
You want some chocolate, buddy?

00:00:56.909 --> 00:00:57.960
Here you go.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.850
It's incredible, really, that the place that
houses a neck-snapping sculpture and a haunted

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:06.180
chess-playing machine could also be the home
of such a delightful little blob.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.229
You know, now that I think of it, it's amazing
that being in the vicinity of unspeakable

00:01:10.229 --> 00:01:14.439
horrors day after day has never put a damper
on 999's positive attitude.

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:18.610
He's got the persistent cheerful disposition
of a labrador puppy.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:24.270
But how well would SCP-999's inherent wholesomeness
hold up against one of the most wicked anomalies

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:27.030
contained by the SCP Foundation?

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:32.630
What would happen if the lightest of the light,
a slimy piece of pure goodness, came up against

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:35.189
deep, dark, evil?

00:01:35.189 --> 00:01:41.060
Not the omnicidal rage of SCP-682, we all
know how that went, but something quieter,

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:42.170
and more menacing.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.229
Well, let's find out...

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:47.479
SCP-999 was having the best day of its life.

00:01:47.479 --> 00:01:51.590
To be fair, every single day was the best
day of the Tickle Monster's life, surpassed

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:54.880
only by the day that followed, and the one
after that.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.229
And how could it not be a good life at the
SCP Foundation, when there were so many friends

00:01:59.229 --> 00:02:03.310
to play with, treats to eat, and so much to
explore!

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:09.500
SCP-999 was enjoying a hearty bowl of M&amp;Ms,
picking out and eating the orange ones, its

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.010
favorites, first, when a familiar figure walked
into its pen.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:17.370
Dr. Jack Bright, who frequently came by to
see the Tickle Monster when he was having

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:21.530
a disappointing day - usually because the
higher-ups had reprimanded him for breaking

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.630
the rules yet again.

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:28.599
SCP-999 cooed delightedly at the sight of
its visitor, slithering over to Dr. Bright

00:02:28.599 --> 00:02:31.420
and enveloping him in an enthusiastic hug.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:36.540
Dr. Bright immediately began to laugh as the
creature's euphoric influence took effect.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:37.540
"Hey!

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.549
Glad there are no hard feelings about that
time I ate a piece of you!"

00:02:40.549 --> 00:02:46.159
He giggled, as 999 patted his face affectionately
with one of its pseudopods.

00:02:46.159 --> 00:02:50.040
"Thanks, that really takes the sting out of
getting the "no chainsaws!"

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.400
hammer brought down on me again."

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:56.550
He patted the slime with his own hand in return,
and, satisfied that it had sufficiently cheered

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:01.739
him, 999 oozed back over to its breakfast
to finish consuming the sugary goodness.

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:02.739
"Oh!

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:03.739
I almost forgot!"

00:03:03.739 --> 00:03:05.860
Dr. Bright pulled something out of his lab
coat pocket.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:10.760
It was a small can of cola, appealingly shiny
in the light.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:11.970
"Want some?"

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:16.209
SCP-999 gurgled curiously, approaching Dr.
Bright to inspect the can.

00:03:16.209 --> 00:03:19.519
He popped it open with an inviting fizz, and
offered some.

00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:22.880
Fortunately, Dr. Rhodes was walking by at
that exact moment.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.610
"Don't you dare!"

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:26.720
She snatched the can out of her colleague's
hand.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.680
"You remember what happened last time.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.340
999 can't tolerate caffeine or carbonation."

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.440
Dr. Bright pouted like a petulant child.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.520
"But I wanted to see it bounce."

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.560
"Do I need to add another rule to the list?"

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:40.560
Dr. Rhodes crossed her arms.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.060
"Or are you going to behave yourself?"

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:46.780
"Fine, whatever, I'll find something else
to do."

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:52.560
Dr. Bright rolled his eyes and left SCP-999's
pen with a final friendly wave at the creature.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.560
Sensing Dr. Rhodes' stress, the Tickle Monster
nuzzled her leg with an inquisitive gurgle.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.329
She smiled indulgently and gave the slime
a hug before she followed Dr. Bright down

00:04:01.329 --> 00:04:06.230
the hall, keeping an eye out for any more
potentially disruptive antics.

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:11.400
Satisfied at having cheered everyone up, SCP-999
went back to its bowl of candy and devoured

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.510
the remaining treats.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:17.500
But then, there was nothing left to eat, and
no one in the room to visit or play with.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.750
What was a lovable slime to do?

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.160
Why, explore, of course!

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:28.590
SCP-999 had the freedom to roam all over the
Foundation site, until bedtime, that is, and

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:33.639
it loved oozing down the halls, looking for
friends to greet and strangers to meet.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:38.120
After all, a stranger is just a friend that
the Tickle Monster hasn't tickled yet.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:42.180
As the slime slid along the floor, it took
the time to say hello to everyone it passed

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:47.340
by bumping them, nudging them, or, in the
case of Josie the half-cat, very gently petting

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.680
her head with one of its pseudopods.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:55.900
The cat purred, and 999 responded by vibrating
its gelatinous body, producing a soft purr

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.000
of its own.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.190
Then Josie was distracted by a dust particle
drifting through a beam of light, and darted

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:02.560
off to chase it.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:07.870
So, the Tickle Monster continued on its way,
looking for something new and fun to do.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:13.009
It spotted the perfect new activity: two guards
were walking into one of the sealed containment

00:05:13.009 --> 00:05:17.310
rooms, a room that the jolly little slime
had never been inside of before.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:22.080
Now was the perfect chance to investigate,
and maybe play tickle wrestling with the guards

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.290
along the way!

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:27.100
It had to act fast, though, the door was beginning
to close.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:32.389
Rearranging its body, 999 squished itself
into a long, thin line, sliding quickly through

00:05:32.389 --> 00:05:35.180
the crack in the door just before it shut.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:40.950
This new room was very messy, much messier
than 999 was allowed to keep its own room.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:45.300
Any spilled chocolate milk or smeared cupcake
frosting was either cleaned up by staff, or

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.639
slurped up by the slime itself.

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:53.380
But in this room, there was thick black liquid
dripping down all of the walls, some of it

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:59.130
arranging itself into patterns and words,
though 999 couldn't read what they said.

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:03.960
The guards hadn't noticed the Tickle Monster's
presence yet, and it kept still, excited to

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:09.830
give them a wonderful surprise when they turned
around and saw that it had followed them inside.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:14.419
But they didn't turn around, they were completely
focused on something in front of them.

00:06:14.419 --> 00:06:15.419
What was it?

00:06:15.419 --> 00:06:19.950
It was a thick glass case that looked as if
it was about to fall apart at any moment.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:26.140
Inside, there was a mask, a porcelain mask
of a frowning face, with that same strange

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:29.060
dark fluid dripping from its eye and mouth
holes.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.259
"You know the procedure, right?"

00:06:30.259 --> 00:06:31.490
One guard said.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.500
He was holding a brand new glass case, shiny
and completely empty.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.660
"Of course I do."

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:38.660
The other scoffed.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.030
"It's my first time with this anomaly, not
my first day on the job."

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:46.180
"Just open it up, take the mask out, and put
it in here," He tapped on the case he was

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:48.570
holding, "As quickly as possible."

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:51.129
"Yeah, I just said, I know."

00:06:51.129 --> 00:06:53.010
The less-experienced guard grumbled.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.479
"Don't patronize me."

00:06:54.479 --> 00:06:57.460
He reached toward the decaying case, and prepared
to unlock it.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:58.810
"Wait...did you hear that?"

00:06:58.810 --> 00:06:59.810
"Hear what?"

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.680
"I thought I heard...never mind."

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:05.070
SCP-999 vibrated with excitement.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.750
Would they give it some well-deserved attention?

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:08.879
Maybe play a game?

00:07:08.879 --> 00:07:12.860
But no, the guard wasn't talking about the
eager orange pal behind him.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:15.670
He was feeling the influence of something
much more sinister.

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:17.370
"Do you want me to do it?"

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.080
The more experienced guard offered.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.080
"No!

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.081
Just...you really don't hear that?

00:07:21.081 --> 00:07:22.349
That whispering?"

00:07:22.349 --> 00:07:24.669
His colleague just shook his head.

00:07:24.669 --> 00:07:27.190
"Fine, just been a long week, I guess."

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:30.949
He sighed, and popped the case open, reaching
for the mask inside.

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:35.060
As soon as his fingers made contact with the
porcelain surface, the black goo dripping

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:39.740
onto his skin where he should have been wearing
protective gloves, his expression shifted.

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:45.210
His eyes went blank, like someone sleepwalking,
lost in a dream even as their body moved in

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:46.210
the waking world.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:47.210
"Frank?

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:48.240
What are you waiting for?"

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:50.950
The other guard nudged him, but Frank said
nothing.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:55.830
He delicately lifted the mask out of the glass
box, and, before anyone could stop him, placed

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.360
the frowning white face over his own.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:00.650
Only it wasn't frowning anymore.

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:06.039
As soon as its features slipped over Frank's,
covering him, erasing him, its mouth curved

00:08:06.039 --> 00:08:07.990
into a malicious smile.

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:10.159
"Frank, what the hell are you doing!"

00:08:10.159 --> 00:08:14.879
The guard cried out, as the man he had once
known grabbed hold of his shoulders.

00:08:14.879 --> 00:08:16.800
"Not Frank anymore."

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.710
A voice came out from between the ceramic
lips, but it was different.

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:23.199
Cruel, cold, ancient.

00:08:23.199 --> 00:08:26.199
"Frank's gone out, I'm afraid.

00:08:26.199 --> 00:08:29.979
And he won't be back any time soon."

00:08:29.979 --> 00:08:34.600
The guard tried to break away from the masked
man's grasp, tried to reach for the emergency

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:39.690
alarm, to signal that the containment change
had gone horribly wrong, but the Mask shoved

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:42.040
him into the wall, hard.

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:46.970
The guard hit his head, and slumped to the
ground, unconscious and likely concussed.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:51.390
Well, SCP-999 had had just about enough of
all this.

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:56.250
It hated seeing anyone hurt, especially humans,
and clearly its help was sorely needed to

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:57.640
make things better.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:02.300
It couldn't tell exactly what had upset the
man in the mask so much that he was acting

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:06.020
this way, but it knew one thing that always
cheered humans up.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:10.010
It was time for a bit of good old-fashioned
tickle wrestling.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:15.580
SCP-999 hurled itself across the room, enveloping
Frank's body from his feet to his neck, and

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:17.770
it began tickling him as it did.

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:22.620
The force of 999's tackle sent Frank's body
careening toward the ground, and when it landed

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.310
with a heavy thud, the mask flew off of his
face and skittered across the floor.

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:33.130
Now that it could see Frank's face, 999 looked
for signs of laughter, of joy, but Frank was

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:36.590
dead asleep, eyes closed, jaw slack.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:39.710
His heart was still beating, but he wouldn't
wake up.

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:45.130
Confused, concerned, and upset at what it
had witnessed in this new room, the slime

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:49.380
slithered along the floor toward the mask
that had caused so much trouble.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:53.020
It seemed to be staring at 999 with its dark,
vacant eyes.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:57.910
It didn't look like a toy, in fact, it looked
like something that the slime should avoid

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:58.910
touching.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:02.840
But it couldn't help but notice that the face
had changed back into a frown.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:07.000
Could 999 really leave the mask there on the
floor, frowning like that?

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.170
The Tickle Monster couldn't help it.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:13.910
With a soft greeting by way of a high-pitched
cooing noise, it reached out to the mask and

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:15.000
picked it up.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:20.160
Though the slime creature didn't have a traditional
face for the mask to sit on top of, its influence

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:23.530
quickly grabbed hold of 999's gelatinous frame.

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:28.120
It stopped moving, stopping gurgling, stopping
looking around at the world through rose-colored

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:29.120
glasses.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:34.460
Right now, SCP-999 was being piloted by The
Possessive Mask, and it was looking for a

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:36.130
way out.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:41.260
Once it escaped containment, it could find
a new host, a proper host, with arms, legs,

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:42.370
and a mouth.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:45.520
But for now, this undignified vehicle would
have to do.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:51.120
It took the Mask some time to learn how to
pilot this strange soft body, with its malleable

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:54.550
form and odd methods of moving itself around
the room.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:59.710
But it slowly adjusted, and, wearing the silhouette
of the Tickle Monster like a disguise, oozed

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:02.790
out of its containment room and into the hall.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:07.590
Staff walking by barely even noticed 999's
presence, they were too preoccupied with their

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:08.590
work.

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:12.050
They were used to seeing it, and giving it
a polite nod, but most of them didn't have

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:15.740
the time to stop and say a proper hello at
this time of day.

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:17.520
Perhaps this would be easy, after all.

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:23.330
The mask had lost its chosen host but found
something even better: the perfect cover,

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:25.930
and the chance to hide in plain sight.

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:30.450
It could take in the lay of the land, scope
out potential exit routes, and ideally slide

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:33.700
out of Foundation custody completely unnoticed.

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:36.570
The mask began to smile at the thought.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:42.000
As the mask steered SCP-999's body around
the Site, a peculiar feeling began to gnaw

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:43.400
at the back of its mind.

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:48.750
Like an itch it couldn't quite scratch, something
irritating wouldn't leave it alone.

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:50.790
What was that feeling?

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:53.770
Inside of its own consciousness, the mask
heard a sound.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:56.340
A sweet, high-pitched gurgle.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:12:02.230
No...that was impossible...and yet, somehow,
the consciousness of the Tickle Monster had

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:05.060
survived in the face of the Mask's power.

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:11.250
It was there, still, needling at the Mask's
darkness with that insipid, insistent kindness.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.730
"Shut up."

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:14.220
The Mask hissed, frowning.

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:18.790
"This body belongs to me now, why won't you
just die?"

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:22.380
Another gurgle, this one even louder, more
difficult to shut out.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.710
Did this infernal thing ever shut up?

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:28.990
The Mask stopped moving for a moment, concentrating
the force of its will.

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:34.070
It would drive SCP-999's mind away and re-establish
dominance.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:39.790
Just as the Mask was grappling with the influence
of SCP-999, however, a familiar figure turned

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:40.940
down the hall.

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:43.300
It was Dr. Rhodes, from earlier!

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:48.270
SCP-999's exuberance bubbled up to the surface,
and the Mask couldn't stop its mouth from

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:50.350
flipping back to a smile.

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:51.350
What?!

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:53.050
No, that was ridiculous!

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:57.370
And yet, the longer the Mask was in contact
with the vibrant orange slime, so delighted

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:03.500
by every familiar and unfamiliar face it encountered,
it could feel that horrible, positive influence

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:06.000
growing stronger and stronger.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:10.380
It was a nauseating, warm, fuzzy feeling that
just made him want to-

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.760
The Mask let out a giggle.

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:18.000
Then another, and before long it was in the
midst of an absolute giggling fit.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:23.170
The Mask had laughed before, it had laughed
plenty of times, but it was usually a mocking

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:24.170
laugh.

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:26.050
A cackle of triumph.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:30.890
This was a giggle of pure joy, the sort of
sound a small child makes as they chase a

00:13:30.890 --> 00:13:32.770
butterfly through a field.

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:37.230
This was the sound of innocence, of happiness,
it was...love.

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:40.790
"Now you listen to me you vile little worm."

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:41.970
The Mask growled.

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:47.220
It wasn't certain if 999 could even understand
it, but it had to show this rebellious creature

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.170
who was really in charge.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.080
"Release your grip on me.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.160
I have won.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.040
You have lost.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:56.520
Your form is mine, and you?

00:13:56.520 --> 00:14:01.480
Nothing more than a puppet for me to pull
on your strings and use you to my own ends.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:04.090
Show some respect and defer.

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:05.150
To.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:06.210
Me."

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:10.680
The voice of the slime creature whimpered
in the Mask's mind, a sound like a chastised

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.880
puppy slinking away with its tail between
its legs.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:15.920
"That's more like it."

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:16.920
The Mask huffed.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:21.140
Dr. Rhodes looked up from her clipboard and
spotted SCP-999.

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:25.940
She waved, about to greet the creature, when
she noticed the horrible mask perched on top.

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:28.960
She dropped her clipboard in shock, gasping
at the sight.

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:29.960
"No..."

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:34.430
She breathed, heart sinking as she saw one
of the purest pieces of good in all of the

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:37.550
Foundation, fallen to the forces of the Mask.

00:14:37.550 --> 00:14:38.930
"That's right."

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:43.100
The Mask would have puffed out its chest,
if this body had a chest to puff.

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:45.190
"I've taken a new host.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:47.750
Do you like my selection?"

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:51.860
It relished the tearful look in the woman's
eyes, the horror that caused her hands to

00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:54.380
shake and her cheeks to go pale.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:15:00.040
"Show me the way to the exit, so that I might
take my leave of this place, and perhaps I

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:02.080
will spare your life..."

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:06.560
The Mask was just gearing up for a good threat,
a really nightmarish one filled with vivid

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:13.290
descriptions of mutilation and violence, when
that disgusting feeling began to rise up again.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:17.000
That warmth...that buoyancy, it made the Mask
want to...

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.020
"Please don't be sad!

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:20.120
Here, let me give you a hug!"

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:24.750
Before it could stop itself, the Mask slithered
the Tickle Monster's body over to Dr. Rhodes,

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.570
wrapping around her tightly.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.250
Not to hurt her, no.

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:29.400
To embrace her.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.600
To comfort her.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:35.870
Her horror turned to laughter, as the mood-lifting
effect of 999's presence began to work its

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:36.870
magic.

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:39.520
Through her laughter, she was also confused.

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:40.920
"Why...?"

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:44.970
She couldn't finish the question, but it was
enough to break the Mask out of the spell.

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:47.290
It reared back, horrified at its actions.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:48.530
"What have I done?

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:49.730
What have I done?!"

00:15:49.730 --> 00:15:53.790
It slithered quickly down the hall, around
the corner, away from that woman who had evoked

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:56.040
such fond feelings toward her.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:59.260
No, toward all of humanity.

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:03.660
The Mask steered its body into a bathroom,
coming face to face with a mirror.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:09.360
It stared at its reflection, its familiar
face and dark eyes, dripping their usual fluid,

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:12.380
perched atop this alien thing poisoning its
mind.

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:14.570
"What did you do to me?

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:16.530
What sort of magic is this?"

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:18.870
Of course, 999 did not answer.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:24.160
But the Mask could feel its presence, could
feel its delight in the impact it was having.

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:25.870
"You're ruining me."

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:26.940
The mask groaned.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:34.020
"I strike terror into hearts, I drive men
to madness, I rend their sanity in two, I..."

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:37.430
it trailed off, overwhelmed again by the urge
to smile.

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:38.430
To laugh.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:39.430
To frolic.

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:43.470
Though it didn't have a working nose, the
Mask could swear it smelled an array of heavenly

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:49.400
scents, of fresh roses, bread baking in a
stone oven, vanilla, and lightly burnt brown

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:50.400
sugar.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:54.690
It reached for itself with its pseudopods,
about to tear itself off of the slimy body

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:56.810
altogether, but it paused.

00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:59.230
"Ah, very clever.

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:01.820
I see what your game is."

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:04.829
It lowered the pseudopods, brimming with determination.

00:17:04.829 --> 00:17:08.699
"You won't trick me into sparing your life.

00:17:08.699 --> 00:17:14.220
Once I've found my freedom, and a host worthy
of me, I will destroy you.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.540
Once and for all."

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:21.010
But even as the Mask made this declaration,
the black liquid seeping from its eyes and

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:24.900
mouth began to change, to take on a lighter
appearance.

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:26.560
Was it a trick of the light?

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.940
No, it was...it was orange.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:33.620
Like the gelatinous flesh of the horrid creature
it had made the mistake of attaching to.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:39.530
No matter how hard the Mask fought, the influence
of SCP-999 was spreading.

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:45.020
Its mind raced, trying to come up with a new
plan, a way to hold onto its identity, but

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:49.190
the sound of an alarm blaring outside the
bathroom spurred it to get a move on once

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:50.190
more.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:53.870
Clearly, Dr. Rhodes had alerted someone that
the Mask had breached containment.

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:57.190
Time was running out, it needed to find the
exit, fast.

00:17:57.190 --> 00:17:58.760
It was now or never.

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:03.280
The Mask oozed back into the hall, speeding
up as it went, trying desperately to find

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:07.810
a way out before whatever transformation had
begun could complete itself.

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:12.150
But even as it struggled, it could feel itself
changing, warping.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:15.560
It burst into giggles again and whistled a
happy tune.

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:20.200
It stopped running for a moment to wave at
an armed guard and blow them a kiss.

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:23.890
Why had it wanted to leave this facility in
the first place?

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:28.830
Everyone here was so kind, was so lovely,
was...its best friend!

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:34.390
No, no...must resist, must not give in to
the optimism, to the happiness...to the goodness…

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:38.590
If the Mask had teeth, it would have been
clenching them, trying to stem the tide of

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:41.190
joyful noises that threatened to burst out.

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:46.600
It felt like...something was tickling it,
and the tickling just wouldn't stop.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:47.620
"Stop it..."

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:49.430
The Mask dissolved into giggles again.

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:50.930
"I mean it..."

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:53.860
It could feel something coming, something
big.

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:58.220
A loud cracking sound rang out, and, just
as the guards were closing in on the possessed

00:18:58.220 --> 00:19:03.290
Tickle Monster, they watched in awe as cracks
spread across the surface of the Possessive

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:07.160
Mask, and, all at once, it shattered into
pieces.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:11.680
The pieces fell to the floor, where they pulled
themselves back together with strands of black

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:12.720
goop.

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:17.880
Meanwhile, SCP-999 sat there, bouncing with
glee, completely unharmed.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:22.480
The Tickle Monster received an extra special
ice cream sundae for its bravery and amazing

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:27.860
work, and the Mask was returned to its containment
chamber, in a brand new glass case.

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:34.130
As the Mask suffered an identity crisis for
the first time in its existence, SCP-999 curled

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:39.210
up in its pen, full of sugar and gratitude,
and got some well-deserved rest.

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:42.840
Now go check out "SCP-999 Tickle Monster VS.

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:45.880
the Most Evil SCPs" and "The Whole Story!

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:49.610
- What if SCP-096 Wore SCP-035?"

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:52.720
for more stories of the Tickle Monster and
the Possessive Mask.

